  is to patrol an area in an unpredictable  way  you have various different types of  specifications  so you want to do a construct correct by  construction synthesis but what are the  specs for that synthesis  so you have a typical type of  specification like maybe  you need to visit each of these various  locations that are important  sufficiently often you know typical type  of spec we could encode in ltl or  something like that  you might also have a constraint like  take a route close to the shortest one  maybe you don't want to take the  shortest one because maybe it's unique  and then there wouldn't be any  unpredictability but it should be fairly  close to the shortest possible route  and then you might have a yet third type  of constraint  saying don't always take the same route  we actually want some unpredictability  in this  and the thing to notice is that these  are three very different types of  constraints  the first is what we call a hard  constraint this is something that has to  be true all the time  whereas this constraint only needs to be  true to some extent  it's sort of a soft constraint and this  third constraint is not a constraint on  individual behaviors at all but it  really it's a constraint on the  distribution of behaviors of the system  so in this application and it turns out  in quite a few other applications so the  couple that i mentioned before  but some others that i won't really get  into in this talk like music  improvisation which is where  the name of this uh problem came from in  the first place  also software fuzz testing other k  things like that  you all they all have this same type of  form if you want to synthesize some  sequence of actions or decisions  something like that subject to three  different types of constraints  a hard constraint which everything you  generate has to satisfy  a soft constraint which most things you  generate have to satisfy  and some randomness constraints saying  you can't just generate the 